1
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:18,690
After you have completed your initial decontamination, preparation, and checks of the BSC, you can

2
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:20,250
begin work.

3
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:23,990
Remember to wear PPE appropriate for the work you will perform.

4
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:29,450
Some groups require that you line your immediate work area with absorbent plastic back material

5
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:34,970
to prevent contamination of the work's surface and facilitate cleanup.

6
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:40,530
That practice is determined by a risk assessment and SOPs, but do not allow this material

7
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:43,810
to block the front or rear air grills.

8
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:50,090
Before loading the BSC, it is a good practice to wipe the external surfaces of all needed

9
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:57,130
supplies with disinfectant to reduce the introduction of outside contaminants into the cabinet.

10
00:00:57,130 --> 00:01:02,450
It is recommended to load necessary materials once in the beginning to minimize your arms

11
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:07,700
entering and exiting while working.

12
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:13,940
Don't forget a biohazardous waste container, sharps container, paper towels, or wipes.

13
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:21,500
Please note, large autoclave pans should only be used in 6-foot or larger BSCs.

14
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:28,100
For smaller BSCs, alternative biohazardous waste containers or bag stands should be used.

15
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:32,900
Remember the clean to dirty principle and place clean materials on one side of the

16
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:38,900
BSC and the biological waste and sharps container on the opposite or dirty side.

17
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:45,540
In this video, we are demonstrating placement of materials for a right-handed person.

18
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:48,660
Materials would be reversed for a left-handed person.

19
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:53,980
Remember to keep the front and rear grills unobstructed to avoid disrupting the airflow

20
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:55,900
in the BSC.

21
00:01:55,900 --> 00:02:00,300
Items should be placed as far back in the cabinet as possible without blocking the rear

22
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:01,300
grill.

23
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:07,060
While working in a BSC, you should be seated and only one person should work in the BSC

24
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,060
at a time.

25
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:13,540
If two people need to work in the BSC at the same time, the BSC must be a minimum of

26
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:19,660
6 feet wide in length and a risk assessment must be performed and documented.

27
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:25,260
Sit down at the BSC and adjust the height of the chair so your face is above the opening

28
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:27,660
and behind the glass.

29
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:33,580
Your arms should be bent at a 90 degree angle at the elbow while inside the BSC.

30
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:38,740
Some BSCs are designed to allow your arms to rest on the front part of the BSC to avoid

31
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:42,580
fatigue or ergonomic injuries over time.

32
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:48,380
Older BSCs that do not have a built-in armrest can be supplemented with a separate armrest

33
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:53,460
that is designed to be placed on the BSC front opening or is attached to the front

34
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:54,460
grill.

35
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:58,900
If used, the BSC should be certified with them in place.

36
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:05,020
Use a foot support if your legs do not reach the floor or if needed for back comfort.

37
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:07,620
Minimize entering and exiting the BSC.

38
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:13,380
If you need to exit and enter the BSC, pull your arms straight out and insert your arms

39
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:14,740
straight in.

40
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:19,340
Perpendicular to the opening, this will minimize air being pulled out of the cabinet

41
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:23,100
and into the breathing zone of the person sitting at the BSC.

42
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:29,140
This is illustrated with a smoke machine in the Factors Affecting BSC Airflow video.

43
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:35,020
Please note, some laboratory SOPs may require you to remove your contaminated gloves and

44
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:40,060
place them in the biohazard container prior to exiting the BSC and put on a new pair

45
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:43,580
of gloves before re-entry.

46
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,380
Be sure to protect the vacuum line.

47
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:51,260
This must include using a HEPA filter and capping unused lines.
